0..75 Comment "//! A truth value in one bit: its layout is a model of the theory of truth."
76..79 Comment "//!"
80..156 Comment "//! A layout stores a value as bits. The bits here are the terms of a theory"
157..230 Comment "//! of one machine bit, and the rules of that theory join some terms. Two"
231..309 Comment "//! terms that a rule joins are one value. So the encoder and the decoder of a"
310..347 Comment "//! layout must agree with the rules."
348..351 Comment "//!"
352..430 Comment "//! The layout is a module that models the theory of truth, and its carrier is"
431..508 Comment "//! the bit terms. The meaning is a module that models the theory of the bit,"
509..585 Comment "//! and each rule is a member that holds a path. The encoder and the decoder"
586..664 Comment "//! are the two folds. Their round trips give an equivalence, and `ua` gives a"
665..696 Comment "//! path between the two types."
697..700 Comment "//!"
701..717 Comment "//! - see: #8288"
